#!/bin/bash
# Old entry point of the scheduled retro run (a crontab line may still name it):
# now retro-run beside it, with the due check once retro.schedule is set. Logs the command that replaces the cron
# line. Removed one release after the alias period.
here=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
if [ "$(uname)" = Darwin ]; then logdir=$HOME/Library/Logs; else logdir=${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}; fi
log=${RETRO_LOG:-${RND_LOG:-$logdir/retro-run.log}}
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$log")"
if [ "$(uname)" = Darwin ]; then hint="set retro.schedule, run \`$here/retro-run --install ${1:-ROOT}\` and remove the cron line"
else hint="point the cron line at $here/retro-run and set retro.schedule (the retro skill's Scheduling)"; fi
echo "$(date '+%F %T') called as ${0##*/}: $hint" >> "$log"
RETRO_LOG=$log exec "$here/retro-run" "$@"
